{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>Lest she weigh</b> — the path of life. <b>She does not know</b> — [refers to] the one being warned, namely 'my sons, attend to my wisdom.'" "<b>Her paths wander</b> — [it is] deficient [in spelling], and likewise נעו רגליו מעגלותיה, or [understood as] her paths wander, by way of metaphor, as if they move about and cause the strange woman to move. But the first interpretation is correct.\n\nAnd likewise the interpretation [of] ארח ('path'), that you set life in it — perhaps you will weigh it and choose it — <b>her paths wander</b>. And the meaning: she goes down to Sheol suddenly, and you do notperceive it until her going down — lest you be chastised and weigh the path of life.\n\nAnother interpretation: in the place where you weigh the path of life, her paths wander, and she does not know."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:21:07.029697435Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}